# Verify before staging push

Complements `auto-commit-staging`. **Do not push broken work to `staging`** hoping CI will catch it.

## Workflow

1. After meaningful work, run **relevant verification** before commit/push.
2. If anything fails → **investigate, fix, and re-run checks**. Repeat until they pass.
3. Only then commit and push to `staging` (per `auto-commit-staging`).
4. If checks cannot pass after reasonable effort, **stop and report the blocker** to the user — do not push.

## Typical verify commands (this repo)

Pick what matches the change; not every task needs every command:

- `npm run build` — default after UI/API client/type changes (`tsc` + Vite)
- `npm run lint` — when lint-related rules or broad refactors touched many files

Report results from **actual command output**, not assumptions (see `shell-autonomy`).

## Safety (unchanged)

- Never commit secrets (`.env`, `prod.env`, live API tokens).
- Never force-push to `main`. No destructive git ops unless the user explicitly requests them.
